The hub rebuilds the subscription: rebranded names, geo-free DNS, its own groups
and rules, its own probe policy. All defensible, all differences, and every
difference is a possible ticket. This site removes the category.

exact (default) — fetch the panel's response for this client and return those
bytes unchanged. No trim, no BOM strip, no CRLF normalisation, no re-encode, no
added comment, no renamed node. Their external-controller, their CN resolvers,
their fallback-filter, their curated rules and GEOIP,CN,DIRECT, their Chinese
group names, their quota pseudo-nodes inside the auto/fallback groups,
skip-cert-verify: false on every node and flow: '' on the ws ones. A Clash client
is pointed at the panel's own YAML switch (type=clash&flag=meta) because that is
how the panel decides what to send; the User-Agent and Accept headers are
forwarded for the same reason. Nothing else is.

safe — the hub's rebuilt profile, fetched from HUB_BASE_URL at request time, not
copied into this repo: a copy of that generator would drift from the one that
customers already use. It is the automatic fallback when the panel answers a bot
challenge or sends something the client cannot import, and it is one parameter
away (?profile=safe) for an app that cannot download geodata.

Everything the hub learned the hard way is carried over, because it applies just
as much to a passthrough: no-store on every response (function responses are
cached by path with the query stripped, so /all/SP VPN is one entry for the whole
site) — and /e/<token> is the recommended link form because a per-customer path
makes that guarantee structural; token resolved before the cache is consulted, so
revocation lands on the next request rather than the next TTL; a store outage
serves the last good file for 24h with X-SPVPN-Stale; a loop-back needs host and
route to match, since a branded domain legitimately serves both; single-flight so
twelve app refreshes are one panel hit; 6.5s + 2.6s budgeted inside the
unconfigurable 10s; and no supplier URL or panel token in any response, ever.

/admin/verify?t= is the reason this is deployable: it fetches our own public URL
and the panel's response independently and diffs them byte by byte, printing the
offset and a window when they differ. `npm test` runs 181 checks against fixtures
with a BOM and CRLF on purpose, and asserts Buffer.compare === 0.

No dashboard, no billing, no renewals: sp-vpn-hub owns the customers. token-store.js
is a verbatim copy of its store client so both hosts read one database, and a link
moves between modes by changing its host.
